# I considered whether A1 bridges "certainty" from full certainty in C1 (no least possibility) to graded certainty "proportioned to our experience" in C.
# I don't count it as a bridge. In S3–S6 both uses rest on experience. The hand-in-fire case is simply the top of that graded scale, equal to the assurance about falling bodies. So the word keeps one sense.
